    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #322\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully.\n\nBranch: `bb/relay-229-agent-runtime-03-08-implement-semp-onl-thr_pi754evzrm`\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #229 in `backend/packages/agent-runtime`:\n\n- **`delegationRegistry.ts`** — `DelegationRegistry`, a process-memory registry of open supervisor→project-agent delegated sessions keyed by `(supervisorRunId, targetProjectItemId)`. A first delegation onto a key opens an `agent_runs` row (`unit='session'`, `triggeredBy='supervisor'`) and an in-process `AgentSession`; a further delegation within 24 hours reuses the same session as a new turn. A duplicate call onto a key already mid-turn is rejected immediately with a fixed busy `tool_result` message, never blocking or overwriting the in-flight call. Busy-check and reservation of a brand-new key both happen synchronously (before any `await`), which closes the race where two concurrent calls onto the same new key would otherwise both try to create a session. After 24 hours of inactivity an in-process timer discards the entry and closes its run as `done` — no backing table or job.\n- **`delegateTool.ts`** — `createDelegateTool` wraps the registry as the `agentTool.delegate` handler, returning only the target's final message (or the busy error) as a `tool_result`-shaped value. Restricting this tool to Semp's own manifest is left to the not-yet-built composition root (#91), the same pattern `startupRepair.ts` used for its own missing caller.\n- **`lifecycleAdapter.ts`** — extracted the turn-processing loop into a reusable `runAgentTurn`, so `runAgentSession` (one turn, closes the run) and the new registry (many turns, closes only on TTL) share identical event bookkeeping.\n- **`types.ts`** — added an optional `AgentSession.send()` continuation method for reusing an open session across turns.\n\nThe branch was rebased onto `origin/develop` to pick up the already-merged parts 01/08 and 02/08.\n\nVerification this run: `pnpm run build` (clean, all 9 packages), `test:unit` (83/83), `test:integration` (441/441, including 8 new tests for the registry and tool), `test:e2e` (5/5), and `check:boundaries` (no violations) — all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
