    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #322\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully.\n\nBranch: `bb/relay-229-agent-runtime-03-08-implement-semp-onl-thr_pi754evzrm` (PR #322)\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed the code review findings from the failed `code-review` CI check on PR #322:\n\n**High severity (2, fixed)**\n- `DelegationRegistry.delegate()` now catches errors from `runAgentTurn` in both the new-session and reused-session branches, closing the `agent_runs` row as `error` (matching `runAgentSession`'s existing pattern) and dropping the broken entry from the registry, instead of leaving the row stuck at `running` forever.\n- `scheduleTtl`'s TTL callback no longer silently drops a rejection: `expire()` now catches its own DB failures internally, logs them, and reschedules a retry instead of losing track of the entry.\n\n**Medium severity (3, fixed)**\n- Added a well-formed-UUID validation on `targetProjectItemId` before it reaches `createAgentRun`'s SQL, since it originates from the model's own untrusted tool-call arguments.\n- Removed the unused, untested `systemPromptOverride` field from `DelegateInput` (out of issue #229's scope).\n- Stopped re-exporting `runAgentTurn`, `extractResultSnapshot`, `pushRunStatus` from the package's public `index.ts` — kept as internal helpers only.\n\n**Low priority**\n- Fixed the `delegateTool.test.ts` blocking fixture to yield `turn_end`.\n- Documented why `lastActivityAt` is kept even though not read internally (issue #229 requires it as an entry field).\n- Added 3 new tests for UUID rejection and error-path cleanup.\n\nVerified this run: `pnpm run build` (clean), `test:unit` (83/83), `test:integration` (444/444), `test:e2e` (5/5), `check:boundaries` (no violations) — all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
