    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #322\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully.\n\nBranch: `bb/relay-229-agent-runtime-03-08-implement-semp-onl-thr_pi754evzrm` (PR #322)\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed the last open medium-severity finding from the code review on PR #322:\n\n**Missing cleanup on send-falsy error path (fixed)**: In `DelegationRegistry.delegate()`'s reused-session branch, the check for `existing.session.send` being missing threw *before* the inner `try/catch` that performs the three-step cleanup (delete entry, clear TTL timer, `failRun`). That left the broken entry in the registry with `busy` reset to `false`, so every subsequent delegation onto that key would hit the same throw until the TTL eventually fired and closed the row as `done` instead of `error`. Moved the check inside the inner `try` so a session that can't continue now goes through the exact same cleanup path as a turn that throws mid-flight.\n\nAdded a new test verifying the run is closed as `error` with the expected message, the entry is fully removed from the registry, and a fresh delegation onto the same key succeeds afterward.\n\nVerified this run: `pnpm run build` (clean), `test:unit` (83/83), `test:integration` (445/445, +1 new test), `test:e2e` (5/5), `check:boundaries` (no violations) — all green.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
